From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: keep the screen saver setting in the registry in the XP session

Purpose: Display Properties' Screen Saver tab shows and stores whether a
screen saver is active, so that the session can start it.
Windows behavior: SPI_GETSCREENSAVEACTIVE and SPI_SETSCREENSAVEACTIVE read
and write the user's setting (HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop,
ScreenSaveActive).
Wine before: winex11 answered both with the X server's own blanking timer
(XGetScreenSaver, XSetScreenSaver): the tab showed and switched Xorg's
blanker, which the XP session turns off because it starts screen savers
itself (session/idle-watch.c).
Change: winex11 does not handle the two actions, so win32u's registry entry
answers them.
Scope: XP session only (the external shell opt-in without WIN4WINE_SHELL).
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@
 #include "xcomposite.h"
 #include "wine/server.h"
 #include "wine/debug.h"
+#include "wine/win4wine.h"
 #include "wine/list.h"
 #include "wine/vulkan.h"
 #include "wine/vulkan_driver.h"
@@ -774,6 +775,12 @@
  */
 BOOL X11DRV_SystemParametersInfo( UINT action, UINT int_param, void *ptr_param, UINT flags )
 {
+    /* win4wine: the XP session starts the screen savers itself, so whether
+     * one is active is the user's setting, not the X server's blanking timer. */
+    if (win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_XP &&
+        (action == SPI_GETSCREENSAVEACTIVE || action == SPI_SETSCREENSAVEACTIVE))
+        return FALSE;  /* win32u keeps ScreenSaveActive in the registry */
+
     switch (action)
     {
     case SPI_GETSCREENSAVEACTIVE:
